TITLE:: PdeBruijn
SUMMARY:: Cyclic coverage of all fixed-length local words
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/PgrayCode, Classes/Pseq, Classes/Pwindow

DESCRIPTION::
Builds a De Bruijn cycle using FKM necklace concatenation, then yields its alphabet objects directly. Each cyclic word of order consecutive symbols occurs once. This covers local subsequences, rather than permutations of an alphabet: repeated symbols within a word are essential. Wrap the cycle around to inspect boundary words. One cycle has alphabet.size raised to order items; cycles exceeding 1000000 items throw before allocation. Memory is O(cycle length + order); generation time is proportional to the generated necklaces and cycle. Objects inside the copied alphabet retain identity. Nil symbols are invalid. All input streams receive the latest inval; finite termination returns it.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: alphabet
Nonempty literal SequenceableCollection of unique non-nil values, copied at stream start.
ARGUMENT:: order
Positive Integer, Function or Pattern sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: repeats
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default 1; sampled once. Zero yields nothing.
ARGUMENT:: rotation
Integer, default 0, sampled once. Output begins at this left offset modulo cycle length; negative values wrap.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
PdeBruijn([0, 1], 3).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Value stream
var values = {
PdeBruijn([0, 1], 3).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x.fold(-7,14) } { 0 }, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical mapping
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \mallet, \degree, PdeBruijn([0, 2, 4, 7], 2), \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Articulation transitions
code::
PdeBruijn([\legato, \staccato, \accent], 2).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Articulation transitions
var values = {
PdeBruijn([\legato, \staccato, \accent], 2).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \saw, degree: 0, dur: 0.2, legato: if(x == \staccato) { 0.2 } { 0.9 }, amp: if(x == \accent) { 0.13 } { 0.06 })
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Short rhythmic cells
code::
PdeBruijn([0.125, 0.25, 0.5], 3).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Short rhythmic cells
var values = {
PdeBruijn([0.125, 0.25, 0.5], 3).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: 0, dur: x, amp: 0.1)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Discrete synthesis combinations
code::
PdeBruijn([[800, 0.1], [2000, 0.3], [4000, 0.6]], 2).collect { |p|
    (cutoff: p[0], rq: p[1])
}.asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Discrete synthesis combinations
var values = {
PdeBruijn([[800, 0.1], [2000, 0.3], [4000, 0.6]], 2).collect { |p|
    (cutoff: p[0], rq: p[1])
}.asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    x.copy.putAll((instrument: \saw, degree: 0, dur: 0.2, amp: 0.07))
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Balanced local musical words
code::
PdeBruijn((0..4), 2).asStream.all.clump(5);
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Balanced local musical words
var values = {
PdeBruijn((0..4), 2).asStream.all.clump(5);
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: if(x.isNumber) { x.fold(-7,14) } { 0 }, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Perceptual-test contexts
code::
PdeBruijn([\quiet, \medium, \loud], 3).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Perceptual-test contexts
var values = {
PdeBruijn([\quiet, \medium, \loud], 3).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: 0, amp: (quiet: 0.025, medium: 0.065, loud: 0.14)[x], dur: 0.25)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Speaker transition test
code::
Pwindow(PdeBruijn([0, 1, 2, 3], 2, 2), 2).asStream.nextN(16);
::

Channel transitions are auditioned as stereo positions. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PdeBruijn / Speaker transition test
var values = {
Pwindow(PdeBruijn([0, 1, 2, 3], 2, 2), 2).asStream.nextN(16);
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \mallet, degree: x[1]*2, pan: x[1].linlin(0,3,-1,1), dur: 0.2, amp: 0.09)
}.play;
)
::
